WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.730
Here's our tax reform plan.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.980
Please implement it at once.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.610
We'll be abandoning the class system 
and implementing a new code of laws.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.950
Any objections?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.480
Good.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.800
Now, for our next reform,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.180
we'll be referring to these...

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.600
Thank you.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.050
You may rest now.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.440
I certainly will.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.500
Did you need something?

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.670
When do you get any sleep?

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.600
Oh, that's all?

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.870
Everyone's saying that the angel of 
the Seven-Light Faith never sleeps.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:56.330
Watching the way you work,
it's easy to believe they're right.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:00.370
Well, I am working you 
nobles-turned-government-officials very hard.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.620
I can't ask that of you and then
go around taking naps, right?

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.540
Don't worry, though. I do get some rest.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.340
I just make it a point to rest 
after the work is done.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.360
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.730
<b>It Seems Lyrule's
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hGrowing Closer to Him!</b>

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.360
He's recovering well.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.640
Man, you're impressive.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.360
His guts were laid out for a moment there,

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.320
and now he's doing so well.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.030
Right?

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:07.070
Ow! You're always so rough!

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.350
I am your daughter, after all!

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.370
Jeez...

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.500
I really owe you a lot, Doctor Keine.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.130
I only did my job as a doctor.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.740
We can't have you sleeping forever.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:24.470
Some big things have happened 
while you were asleep.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.200
Yeah, our village picked a 
fight with the Empire, for one.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.800
You missed out on something really cool!

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.810
I need to heal up quickly
and join the next battle!

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.580
If you plan on overexerting yourself,

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.240
I'll have you go back to sleep
for a while longer.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.800
Good grief.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.950
Please take better care of your body.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.820
Sorry.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.140
Roo?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.440
What's the matter?

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.880
One times five is... five.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.520
I'm alive again!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.190
What have you been doing, 
going without food or water?

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:17.560
My teacher's giving me a multiplication test,

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.320
so I'm trying to memorize this tables thing.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.620
"Tables thing"?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.460
It's a song about multiplication.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.860
Memorizing it helps make 
learning multiplication easier.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.330
Multiplication, huh.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.160
Multiplication, huh?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.830
I'm not great at it, either.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.330
You'll be fine, Roo!

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.210
You can make a living just fine 
without knowing how to multiply!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.360
Uh-huh! Just like us!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.640
<i>Good examples of bad adults...</i>

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.810
My teacher told me tables are 
a merchant's foundation.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.180
But I just can't memorize them at all...

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.260
The basics are important in everything.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.780
So you'll just have to 
keep at it and study more.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.640
Looks like the power plant's
coming along well.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.080
We managed to secure a large 
amount of coal, too.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.120
I'm storing the power it generates 
in high-capacity batteries

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.470
taken from our miniature nuclear reactor.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.970
<i>We'll be starting the 
trial run tomorrow, bear!</i>

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:35.600
Then that takes care of our
power generation issue.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.230
Thank you, Ringo.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:44.910
In that case, I'll move on 
to the next project, okay?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.200
I'm counting on you.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.300
<i>Bye-bye, bear!</i>

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:52.830
Next project?

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:57.340
The production of machine tools 
like a lathe and a milling machine.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.100
For the battles in spring,

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.960
I'm planning to equip a portion
of our squads with guns.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.110
Modernizing our military, huh?

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.840
Wait, why not build an automatic 
manufacturing plant?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.440
Well, I'd like the people of this 
world to make guns and gunpowder

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.970
with their own hands as much as possible.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.200
This is their fight, after all.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.230
I see.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.620
If we just handed them
freedom on a silver platter,

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:21.930
it wouldn't mean anything.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.230
Exactly.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:29.980
Besides, we need Ringo to construct an 
aerial defense system as quickly as possible.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.220
Aerial defense?

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.240
You think missiles are going 
to fly our way? In this world?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.740
This world has its own version of
aerial warfare, with magic and dragons.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:42.120
We need to be wary of the skies.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:45.250
Besides, I received a 
curious report from Shinobu.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:47.560
Heaven's Flames?

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:48.670
<i>Uh-huh!</i>

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:53.680
It's a tactical spell with the force
to obliterate an entire city.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.680
The governor of the northern lands,
Oslo El Gustave,

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.470
used Heaven's Flames in the previous war,

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.560
creating seas of fire in the cities
of his enemy's nation.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.190
The governor of the northern lands, huh?

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.280
Sounds like there's a strong possibility

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.200
he'll chuck this Heaven's Flames 
at us here, in Dormundt.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.270
Exactly.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.790
Tsukasa!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.220
Lyrule?

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.910
Didn't you go back to Elm Village
with Winona and the others?

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.880
Well, this whole war started because of me,

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.530
so I wanted to be useful 
to you all in some way.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:32.130
Which is why I'm helping to 
distribute food right now.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.760
I see.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.470
Thank you. This is a big help.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.930
Um, Tsukasa?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.680
What is it?

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.310
If you wouldn't mind,

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:46.440
could we have lunch together?

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:51.450
I wanted to thank you properly for saving me.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:57.200
I appreciate the offer, but I'll 
just accept the sentiment for now.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.940
I have a meeting I need to attend,

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.340
so I have to head back right away.

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:11.240
Masato, do you think Tsukasa hates me?

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:14.280
No way. He's just busy.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.800
You think so?

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:20.430
I get the feeling
he's keeping me at a distance.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.180
Lyrule...

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.280
I suppose he must be mad.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.800
Since I did trigger this war...

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.190
That's not true.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.100
Then does he find my ears creepy?

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.380
Calm down.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.790
Everything's fine.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.180
But, but...

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:40.120
It's honestly not something 
to cry over like that!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.160
But I'm so worried...

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.360
Look, he's just having trouble 
facing you because he feels guilty.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.330
Huh?

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.500
When everyone in the village
wanted to rescue you,

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.520
he was the only one who spoke up
to suggest abandoning you.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.150
I didn't know that...

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.050
Please don't get the wrong idea, though.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:12.730
It wasn't because he didn't <i>want</i> to save you.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.530
He made that suggestion out of concern
for the village as a whole.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:19.280
Yes, I understand.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:27.000
He always prioritizes
the happiness of the majority,

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:31.460
even when that would mean 
sacrificing those precious to him.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.350
It's something I'll never understand.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:37.150
To be frank, I think he's crazy.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.930
But, well, you know!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:44.180
That idiot's just lost in himself, so leave
him be for a while and he'll be fine.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.810
I'm sorry.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.680
You asked for building-age assessments,

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:56.830
but the craftsmen that accompanied us said
they couldn't make them any more precise.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:57.450
Okay.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.600
This is important information for 
urban development and improvement.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.580
You did a good job on this difficult task.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.270
You can take tomorrow off.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.800
Get some rest.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.540
Thank you very much!

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.050
I guess I've been pushing myself too hard.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.290
Who is it?

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.470
It's me, Lyrule.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.230
Do you have some time right now?

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.880
I'm sorry, but I have a busy day tomorrow,

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.400
so I was planning to turn in early tonight.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.440
Could you come back some other time?

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.670
I understand.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:42.510
If you're about to sleep, then you're 
done with work for today, right?

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.450
Huh?

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.790
Pardon me!

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.660
I-Is this something that urgent?

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.290
Yes. Please let me repay you.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.460
Repay me, you say?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.300
Any way is fine.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.800
I'm willing to do anything I can!

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.440
You don't need to.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:12.770
I tried to abandon you.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.350
I know.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.360
But that doesn't matter.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:23.360
If putting up with it all by myself meant 
saving everyone else in the village,

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:25.860
then that's what I would have wanted, too.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:26.740
Yet...

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.750
despite that, you still came to save me.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.150
So please let me thank you. at least.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.300
I'm not the kind of man you think I am.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.220
That's not true!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.520
You're a very kind person!

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:53.900
You gave us mayonnaise, 
thinking of the children.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.270
You were also the one who 
drove off those violent men!

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.820
Even when the Chief of the Forest attacked,

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.280
you thought about everyone in Elm Village!

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:04.780
You're...

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.530
You're a good person!

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:16.210
I killed my own father, you know.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:38.890
When I was young, I admired 
my father, a politician.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.900
However, one day I discovered something.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:45.520
I discovered that his power

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:49.100
was built upon such corruption
that I wished I'd never found out.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:55.700
I couldn't forgive my father for
deceiving the people and abusing his power.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:13:01.420
<b>Former Prime Minister Mikogami Arrested</b>

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.360
I worked with Shinobu and the Merchant
to expose my father's wrongdoing.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.420
He was put to trial

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.910
and sentenced to death.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:12.220
You must be insane!

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:17.610
In prioritizing justice for the people,

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:21.150
I had, in fact, driven my father to his death.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.280
My mother still hates me for what I did.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.400
Of course she would.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:34.790
Even if my father committed those crimes,
he was still the man she loved.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:35.980
However,

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:40.470
I can't forgive my father for what he did.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:47.670
Why are <i>you</i> crying?

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.720
I'm sorry. I...

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.400
Just thinking about how you must have felt...

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.710
made me so sad...

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:59.730
How could you go that far? Doesn't it hurt?

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:03.730
It does.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.060
But I don't regret it.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.740
Because the type of politician 
I'm striving to be

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:15.050
is one only possible for a selfless saint.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.220
Tsukasa...

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:21.550
I'm sorry.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:23.550
That wasn't a very pleasant story.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:32.550
Lyrule?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.950
Tsukasa, you are selfish.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:38.980
You're feeling guilt of your own making 
and distancing yourself from me.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:43.980
You might believe it's only 
natural for me to hate you now,

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:47.820
but I'll never let it turn out that way!

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.700
I won't ever hate you, Tsukasa!

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:04.590
You win. I give in.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.590
You mean...

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:11.090
Then I'm going to have you 
take on a slightly difficult task.

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:12.590
Brace yourself for it.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:13.690
Huh?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:22.100
Um, Tsukasa, wh-what is...?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.980
You did say you'd do anything for me.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:29.610
I should be able to get three hours 
worth of rest in an hour like this.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.320
O-Okay, then. You can sleep 
here all night, not just one hour!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.160
That will wear your legs out.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:41.030
You can wake me up if they start to hurt.

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:42.080
Yes.

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:58.140
Thank you, Lyrule.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.240
Huh?

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.220
For crying for me.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:04.860
It made me feel a little better.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:06.660
Sure.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:27.230
<i>Huh? Ringo?</i>

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:31.510
<i>Huh? Are you already done 
talking to Tsukasa?</i>

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:34.380
<i>Hey, Ringo, I thought you were 
going to hand over the material list</i>

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.940
<i>and consult him on the production system?</i>

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.390
<i>I don't think you were in there 
long enough to do that, bear!</i>

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.660
<i>Were you not able to talk to him, bear?</i>

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:45.520
<i>Do you need me to come 
with you, bear, bear, bear?</i>

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:05.930
One times four is four. 
One times five is five. One times six is...

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.380
I don't understand tables at all!

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.420
Do not look this way, okay?!

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.720
I understand, so please make it quick.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:21.510
Oh, you're both here?

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:24.270
Hey?! Wh-Why is Keine here, too?!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.480
Oh, shut up and quit dawdling!

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.580
Would you just get in already?!

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:36.520
I'm a child of Edo, so I hate 
babbling and dawdling the most!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.810
Man, I didn't expect you to be here, Roo.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.660
Are you hurt?

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.670
No, just a little surprised.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:54.170
This is all Akatsuki's fault
for being stubborn.

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.980
This isn't right!

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:58.680
Why are you following me into the bath, too?!

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:02.250
You're the founder 
of the Seven-Light Faith.

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:04.890
In a sense, that makes you our lord.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:09.190
So, naturally, you must be
accompanied by a guard at all times.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:13.190
Th-Then it still isn't right for Keine 
to get in the same bath with me!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:18.570
Oh? I don't particularly mind.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.140
I'm done.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:26.490
Roo, you seem kind of down.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.710
I can't memorize the tables...

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.960
You mean multiplication tables?

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:37.720
I need to pass my teacher's 
test on multiplication.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.040
I see.

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:41.720
You're training to be a merchant, aren't you?

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.220
She's apprenticed to Masato.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:50.340
Numbers just get all fuzzy and 
they won't go in my head...

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:57.150
Watching Roo work hard like that 
reminds me of my own training days.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:03.160
I was all fed up when they had 
me just repeating sword forms.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.390
Ah, I know what you mean.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:08.410
Practicing magic was nothing 
but repetition, too.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:13.340
Since I already knew the trick, 
it wasn't any fun at all.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.880
That's true.

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:20.520
I had to memorize whole books
on anatomy and medicine.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:26.040
How did you all manage to push through it?

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:30.790
I had started learning the Ichijou Style 
of swordsmanship from a very young age...

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.400
but one day I found a goal for myself.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.150
A goal?

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.730
I fell in love with a samurai drama called 
<i>The Much Too Unfettered Shogun</i>.

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:42.660
I wanted to become someone who could 
aid the powerless with their sword.

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:45.660
And you two?

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.520
Well, when I was in elementary school,

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:50.970
I had a feeling that this 
was the only thing for me.

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:55.170
I wonder what my goal is...

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.770
It's not that difficult to figure out.

00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:01.170
It's basically what you want to do.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:05.680
When there's something you want to do, 
all that's left is to work hard at it, right?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.310
What I want to do?

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.230
There is something I want to do!

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.200
I'm going to work hard, too!

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:18.230
I'm going to work hard, memorize the tables, 
and defeat multiplication!

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.740
Indeed! That's the spirit!

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.910
I know. What's something you like, Roo?

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.280
Money!

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.640
O-Oh... Well, that works, too.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.310
Numbers just tend to be a little abstract,

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:33.710
so why don't you try imagining 
money while doing your math?

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:36.460
Imagine money?

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:37.210
Yeah.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:41.980
So for five times five, that would mean 
you have five stacks of five gold coins.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.020
I know that! That's 25 coins!

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.720
I understand!

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:47.950
My!

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.420
R-Really?

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.720
Then how about seven times seven?

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:55.530
Forty-nine coins!

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:57.150
Huh, correct.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.420
Then eight times nine?

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:02.170
Seventy-two coins!

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.280
Seriously?!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:04.360
Th-Then...

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.490
Twenty-four times three hundred sixty-five!

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.670
8,760 coins!

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:12.250
C-Correct!

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.500
I did it!

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.750
I did it!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:20.380
I conquered multiplication!

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:31.520
Uh, Roo should've passed her 
multiplication test, right?

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:32.600
Surely.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:36.600
Then why does she look 
like she's dead inside?

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.660
Apparently, her next test is division.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:40.810
Ah...

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:44.240
The path to becoming a merchant is perilous.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:48.340
Roo's coins keep going away...

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.800
I'm scared of division...

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.700
Listen, El.

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:31.930
This...

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:35.680
is the truth behind this village.

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:39.270
What is this?
